// BEFORE (correct): reject the batch if it is not fully valid
if (!items.every(isValid)) reject(batch);

// AFTER review suggestion 'cleaner without the bang':
if (items.every(i => !isValid(i))) reject(batch);

// Production: a batch with 99 valid items and 1 corrupted item sailed through.

The BEFORE condition is true when ______ (b1) item is invalid (¬∀ = ∃¬).
The AFTER condition is true only when ______ (b2) items are invalid.
The correct negation-preserving rewrite is items.______ (b3)(i => !isValid(i)).

